  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Contributing to a more Gender- responsive National Police in Colombia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To Contribute to a more gender-responsive Colombian Nacional Police through an institutional gender self-assessment. The Colombian National Police has expressed willingness to undertake this gender self-assessment with the support and guidance of DCAF and CIASE. 
The gender self- assessment includes eight geographical regions of the Colombian National Police and ensures inclusion of police satff from regional territories into the self-assessment. 

After an institutional gender self-assessment undertaken by the Colombian Nacional Police (CNP), the project seeked to turn the CNP into a gender-responsive security sector institution.
The CNP meets the different security needs of women &amp; men and promotes equal participation (roles &amp; responsi-bilities) of women &amp; and men within the institution, through reinforcement of gender-responsive governance capacities at institutional, unit and regional level.</narrative>
  </description>
